From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:42:29 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: drop the blind RCU watchdog-reset write

cbm_hw_init() reproduces three register values from the vendor system's
boot state before touching the datapath. Two of them, the NGI endian mask
and the interface mux, belong there: they are sampled at block reset and
have to be in place before anything in this driver resets anything.

The third does not. RCU_IAP_WDT_RST_EN gates the GIC per-VP watchdog's
reset request; it was written here only because the vendor system has it
set and this driver was the earliest place to reproduce that. It has no
bearing on the ethernet datapath, and now that intel_grx500_wdt owns the
watchdog it owns this register too. Two uncoordinated writers to one word
is how the chiptop endian mask went wrong for two phases.

Nothing else observes the register, so the only configuration this
changes is CONFIG_INTEL_GRX500_WDT=n, where nobody writes it -- and there
is no watchdog to arm.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
index 921902455b53..c50dcc55d514 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
@@ -275,12 +275,13 @@ int cbm_hw_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * Endian straps are sampled at block reset, so the value must be held
-	 * across the whole datapath bring-up.
+	 * The datapath initiators must be strapped big-endian before any CBM
+	 * or GSW reset: the straps are sampled at block reset, so the value
+	 * has to be held across bring-up. SPI_DEBUG_EN (IFMUX_CFG bit 18) is
+	 * cleared as the vendor's own chiptop setup does.
 	 */
 	{
 		void __iomem *ct = ioremap(0x16080000, 0x200);
-		void __iomem *rcu = ioremap(0x16000000, 0x100);
 
 		if (ct) {
 			u32 pre;
@@ -290,11 +291,7 @@ int cbm_hw_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			__raw_writel(pre & ~(BIT(22) | BIT(18)), ct + 0x120);
 			iounmap(ct);
 		}
-		if (rcu) {
-			__raw_writel(0x0000000F, rcu + 0x50);
-			iounmap(rcu);
-		}
-		pr_info("cbm: chiptop/RCU parity applied (ipt_endian, ifmux, wdt_rst_en)\n");
+		pr_info("cbm: chiptop parity applied (ipt_endian, ifmux)\n");
 	}
 
 	(void)pdev;
